  "kind": "statement",
  "title": "Valuative extension to a proper separated morphism",
  "statement": "Let $f\\colon Y\\to S$ be proper and separated. Every commutative square\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Spec}(K)\\longrightarrow Y\n\\qquad\\text{over}\\qquad\n\\operatorname{Spec}(A)\\longrightarrow S\n$$\n\nwith $A$ a valuation ring and $K=\\operatorname{Frac}(A)$ admits a unique\nlift $\\operatorname{Spec}(A)\\to Y$.",
  "source": {
    "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-nagata-compactification/sk-thm-nagata-sketch-two-open/lemma-nagata-proper-separated-valuation-extension.md",
    "place": "node lemma-nagata-proper-separated-valuation-extension, order 297"
  },
  "stmt_deps": [],
  "proof": [
    {
      "text": "Existence is the output of\n[lemma-nagata-proper-valuative-criterion-existence-api]. If $h$ and\n$h'$ are two such lifts, their generic restrictions are the prescribed\nmorphism, so\n[lemma-nagata-separated-valuation-lift-unique] gives $h=h'$. Thus the\nextension exists and is unique.",
      "uses": [
        "lemma-nagata-proper-valuative-criterion-existence-api",
        "lemma-nagata-separated-valuation-lift-unique"
      ],
      "elementary": false
    }
